 cache←Build opt;CountTerms;Stem;dt_fields;ep;mat_fields;norm;pid;pname;search_fields;stemmer;term_count;title;vids;weights;ytid
 ;GetEnv;ReadJSON;Unidecode;SQL;Table2JSON;TimeStamp2DDN
⍝ The external dependencies above are localised so that Setup's assignments appear as
⍝ Build's locals and vanish on return, otherwise certain names (e.g. .NET class instances)
⍝ prevent the CACHE namespace from being serialised into isolate processes.
⍝ opt: using and app_dir, computed in the main process
⍝ cache: cache namespace for wholesale replacement
⍝ Store pre-joined tables for API endpoints and query results
⍝ Create character and numeric matrices for filters
⍝ Compute BM25F score matrix for search
⍝ Compute cosine similarity matrix for recommendations

⍝ One day we'll have modules and do ⎕IMPORT'SQL' etc. Not today.
⍝ CACHE.Build is callable from the main process and in an isolate. CACHE.Setup imports dependencies into the CACHE namespace.
 {}Setup opt

 'cache'⎕NS''

 ep←ReadJSON opt.app_dir,'APLSource/QUERY/endpoints.json5'

 cache.presenters←Table2JSON ep.presenters.fields⍪SQL.Do ep.presenters.sql

 'cache.events'⎕NS''
 cache.events.data←Table2JSON ep.events.fields⍪SQL.Do ep.events.sql
⍝ has_videos is a derived column for filtering events with and without videos
⍝ returned in the API response as enclosed string which translates to JSON boolean values
⍝ stored in APL as numeric 0 and 1 for efficient filtering
 :If 0=≢cache.events.data
     cache.events.has_videos←⍬
     cache.events.data←⍬
 :Else
     cache.events.has_videos←cache.events.data.has_videos
     cache.events.data.has_videos←⊂¨'false' 'true'[1+cache.events.has_videos]   ⍝ Convert APL Bool to JSON Bool
 :EndIf

 vids←cache.videos←⎕NS''   ⍝ Namespaces pass by reference, so assignment to vids shorthand updates cache namespace

 vids.fields←ep.videos.fields
 vids.values←SQL.Do ep.videos.sql
 (title ytid pname pid)←↓⍉SQL.Do ep.videos.presenter.sql   ⍝ YouTube ID, presenter name
 :If 0<≢vids.values
     (ytid pname pid)←↓⍉ytid{(pname pid)←↓⍉⍵ ⋄ ⍺,(⊃(⊣,', ',⊢)/pname)(pid)}⌸⍉↑pname pid
 :EndIf
 vids.values,←(pname,⊂'')[ytid⍳vids.values[;vids.fields⍳⊂'youtube_id']]
 vids.values,←(pid,⊂⍬)[ytid⍳vids.values[;vids.fields⍳⊂'youtube_id']]

 :If (≢vids.fields)≠⊢/⍴vids.values
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 400)('Vendor' 'DCMS')('Message' 'endpoints.json5 videos endpoint number of fields does not match number of columns')
 :EndIf

⍝ For indexing, normalise all except those with YouTube IDs and convert datetimes to Dyalog Day Number
 vids.values⌷⍨←⊂⍒vids.values[;vids.fields⍳⊂'presented_at']   ⍝ Given equal rankings, prefer recent videos
 vids.index_all←vids.values

⍝ Normalise text fields
 (norm/vids.index_all)←Unidecode.NormaliseText¨(norm←vids.fields(~∊)⊆'presented_at' 'published_at' 'url' 'youtube_id' 'thumbnail' 'presenter_id')/vids.index_all

⍝ Format numeric and datetime fields
 dt_fields←vids.fields⍳⊆'presented_at' 'published_at'
 vids.index_all[;dt_fields]←TimeStamp2DDN vids.index_all[;dt_fields]
 vids.index_cols←↓⍉vids.index_all
⍝ Store fields as matrices for filter queries
 mat_fields←vids.fields⍳⊆'youtube_id' 'presenter_id'
 vids.index_cols[mat_fields]←↑¨vids.index_cols[mat_fields]

⍝ Tokenise search fields
 search_fields←'title' 'event' 'event_shortname' 'description' 'youtube_id' 'presenter'
 weights←2 2 1 2 1 3
 stemmer←⎕NEW Porter2Stemmer.EnglishPorter2Stemmer
 Stem←{
     stemmed←stemmer.Stem⊆⍵
     stemmed.Value
 }

 CountTerms←{
     text←{('  '∘⍷~⍛/⊢)(⎕UCS 10 13)~⍨,⍕⍵}¨⍵
     words←(⎕C ⎕A)∘(∊⍨⊆⊢)¨text
     non_words←(' ',⎕C ⎕A)∘(~⍤∊⍨⊆⊢)¨text
     w_index←∪⊃,/,words
     find_words←w_index∘⍳¨words
     w_count←¯1+↑{{≢⍵}⌸(⍳≢w_index)⍪⍵}¨find_words
   ⍝ Only stem the unique index words to reduce number of calls to .NET. Stemmer package
   ⍝ FIXME modify package to accept a list of words, else implement in Dyalog
     new←w_index≢¨stems←Stem¨w_index
     w_count,←new/w_count   ⍝ Count of stemmed words is count of original words
     w_index,←new/stems
    ⍝ Add non_word term counts
     nw_index←∪⊃,/,non_words
     find_nw←nw_index∘⍳¨non_words
     nw_count←¯1+↑{{≢⍵}⌸(⍳≢nw_index)⍪⍵}¨find_nw

     index←↑w_index,nw_index
     term_count←w_count,nw_count
     index term_count
 }

 (vids.index term_count)←CountTerms(vids.fields∊search_fields)/vids.index_all

 vids.search←vids.index ComputeSearch weights term_count
 vids.recommendations←ComputeRecommendations vids.search
